#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:36
msgid "Alerts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:51
msgid "New Administrator Alert"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:53
msgid "Send an email whenever an account gains administrator privileges, or an existing administrator account is modified — no matter how it happened: the admin screens, a plugin, the REST API, WP-CLI, or a direct write into the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:58
msgid "Enable Alerts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:64
msgid "Email me when a new administrator appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:65
msgid "Works independently of the main firewall switch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:72
msgid "Notification Email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:78
msgid "Account Takeover"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:84
msgid "Also alert when an existing administrator is modified"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:85
msgid "Watches the username, email address and password of every administrator. Rewriting an admin's email address is how an account is seized — it hands over the password reset flow while the user ID stays the same, so watching for new accounts alone would never see it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:92
msgid "Database Scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:98
msgid "Hourly scan for administrators created outside WordPress"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:99
msgid "Compares the live administrator list against a stored snapshot. This is what catches accounts inserted straight into the database, created by code that bypasses the WordPress user API, or added while this plugin was inactive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:105
msgid "Save &amp; run scan now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:108
msgid "Save &amp; send test email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:117
msgid "How detection works"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:121
msgid "WordPress hooks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:123
msgid "Immediate. Catches every account creation or role change that goes through the WordPress user API — the Users screen, user registration, the REST API, WP-CLI, and any plugin or theme calling wp_insert_user() or set_role(). The alert names the acting user and their IP address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:127
msgid "Database scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:129
msgid "Within the hour. A snapshot of every administrator user ID is stored, and the scheduled scan diffs it against the live list. Anything that appears without a hook firing — a direct SQL INSERT, a modified wp_capabilities meta row, an account added while the plugin was off — shows up here and is flagged as created outside the normal WordPress flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:133
msgid "What the snapshot stores"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:135
msgid "Per administrator: the user ID, the username, the email address, and a digest of the stored password hash. The digest only ever answers \"did this change?\" — the password itself is never stored, never compared and never printed in an alert."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:139
msgid "No duplicate alerts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:141
msgid "Both paths write to the same snapshot, so each event is reported exactly once. Existing administrators are recorded silently when the feature is turned on — you are only told about what happens afterwards. Removing an administrator is not reported; the account simply leaves the snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:165
msgid "Separate multiple addresses with commas. Leave empty to use the site admin email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:184
msgid "The last alert email could not be sent. Check your site mail configuration (SMTP plugin, hosting mail limits) — an alert that never arrives is no alert at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:192
msgid "Administrators tracked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:198
msgid "Alerts go to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:204
msgid "Snapshot taken"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:205
msgid "never — taken on the first scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:210
msgid "Next scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/TabAlerts.php:211
msgid "not scheduled"
msgstr ""

